<title>UK: German inland gas oil softens in weak demand.</title>
<headline>German inland gas oil softens in weak demand.</headline>
<text>
<p>(DLR/DM=1.4773     DM/100 LTRS  DLRS/100 LTRS  LAST DM</p>
<p> HAMBURG		    33.00/33.10  22.33/22.40    33.30/33.40</p>
<p> BREMEN		     33.00/33.10  22.33/22.40    33.30/33.40</p>
<p> DUISBURG		   33.10/33.20  22.40/22.47    33.30/33.40</p>
<p> FRANKFURT		  33.40/33.70  22.60/22.81    33.70/33.80</p>
<p> KARLSRUHE		  33.90/34.20  22.94/23.15    34.10/34.20</p>
<p> INGOLSTADT		 34.80/35.10  23.56/23.75    35.00/35.20</p>
<p>German inland gas oil prices were weaker on Tuesday amid weak demand. Traders said prices had softened throughout the day in line with lower benchmark futures and lack of end-user demand. -- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7714</p>
</text>
